From a0a2f369a9bbcb33dc73d0837edb628997d587cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:44:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: @ popover spans spaces for multi-word
 sources (@demo bear)

An @ token ended at the first space, so a session mention typed by title
('@demo bear') closed the popover at '@demo'. A composer.atCompletions
source can now declare multiWord: while the open @ popover holds a row
from such a source, typing a space widens the same token (continueAtTrigger,
max 6 words, never across a newline/@/chip, never for @file:-style scopes)
and the source receives the spaced query. When the settled answer has no
multi-word row the popover closes immediately, so prose after '@name '
behaves as before. Sources without the flag never see a space.

Tests: use-composer-trigger-multiword.test.ts (widen, close-on-no-match,
pick replaces whole token, non-multiWord control, Escape control,
continueAtTrigger guards) + contrib metadata tag test. 9/9 condition
mutants killed. Composer suite 103 files green; tsc + eslint clean.
Docs: desktop-plugin-sdk.md atCompletions.multiWord.
